<title>USA: Neurobiological COO Ostrach resigns.</title>
<headline>Neurobiological COO Ostrach resigns.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Calif. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Neurobiological Technologies Inc Monday said Michael Ostrach has resigned as executive vice president, chief operating officer, secretary and member of the board of directors.</p>
<p>The company said Ostrach, who joined the company in 1994, is leaving to pursue opportunities with biomedical firms focused primarily on discovery research.</p>
<p>Ostrach will continue to serve as a business development consultant to the company while Neurobiological conducts a search for a vice president for the business development function. The company said it will not fill the chief operating officer position.</p>
